  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "NT-ENTITY-01",
      "priority": "P1",
      "title": "Native and pointer selection leave contradictory entity readouts",
      "status": "REPRODUCED_PRE_FIX",
      "symptom": "Pointer select tool workSurface.trace, then native-select actor trace-coach. The owned producing-event readout changes, while the vendor entity/count/visits panel keeps the tool.",
      "cause": "Owner selectedId and vendor selected message are separate state; native selection never updates the vendor state.",
      "evidence": [
        "E6c-nodetrace-independent-host/pointer-then-native-other.png",
        "E6c-nodetrace-independent-host/pointer-then-native-other.json"
      ],
      "nextProof": "Pointer to native to clear to a new selection must update every readout to the same current entity in source and installed consumer."
    },
    {
      "id": "NT-ENTITY-02",
      "priority": "P1",
      "title": "Same-ID data growth leaves old visit metadata",
      "status": "REPRODUCED_PRE_FIX",
      "symptom": "After replacing six traces with twelve using new event IDs and unchanged entity identities, the selected tool has two producing events but its visits panel stays at one.",
      "cause": "The vendor reads mutable graph attributes during render before its effect patches attributes; same-ID changes do not increment rev, so there is no follow-up render for the changed visit count.",
      "evidence": [
        "E6c-nodetrace-independent-metadata-replay/same-entities-extra-events.png",
        "E6c-nodetrace-independent-metadata-replay/same-entities-extra-events.json"
      ],
      "nextProof": "Retain selection across same-ID props replacement; event IDs and visit count must both describe the new snapshot without another user action."
    },
    {
      "id": "NT-ENTITY-03",
      "priority": "P1",
      "title": "Removing the hovered node leaves the whole graph dimmed",
      "status": "REPRODUCED_PRE_FIX",
      "symptom": "After removing the currently hovered tool, the remaining twelve entities all turn grey and labels disappear. Pointer-out and Fit do not recover the state.",
      "cause": "The renderer closure retains hoverRef.current after that ID disappears from the graph. Every remaining node fails the stale-neighbor predicate and is dimmed; the stale hover is not cleared by the graph patch.",
      "evidence": [
        "E6c-nodetrace-independent-hover-isolation/hovered-entity-removed.png",
        "E6c-nodetrace-independent-hover-isolation/removed-entity-pointer-out.png",
        "E6c-nodetrace-independent-hover-isolation/removed-entity-fit.png"
      ],
      "nextProof": "Remove/replace the hovered entity during the same mount, keep the pointer still, then move out and Fit; remaining nodes and labels must return to their normal state."
    }
  ],
  "proofLimits": [
    "Component-host proof uses exact copied application/vendor files, the actual six-event source fixture, an isolated anonymous Chromium context at 390x844 and reduced motion. It is not a complete source-app or installed-consumer review.",
    "The chroma-only painted-ring helper falsely described grey visible nodes as an empty canvas. Raw failures and actual pixels are preserved; no WebGL crash was observed.",
    "The dense fixture had 160 entities from 40 synthetic traces within the stated input bounds. Full native identity wrapping, document bounds and pan/Fit were observed, but its canvas labels were suppressed and the hover target was not semantically confirmed. Positive dense label/hover proof is still required.",
    "All tested empty states removed stale visible readouts; reintroduced same identities used current producing-event IDs, but the independent vendor panel remained subject to the selection/metadata defects above.",
    "No primary source/index/ref/build/public-fixture mutation, credentials, production request or port 4173 was used. Root was told the original-source read guard could close after the immutable copy was established.",
    "Final source, installed consumer, normal-motion seven-width matrix and fixed-state review are pending. No final product grades are granted."
  ],
